WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Regulatory steps in South Africa and India move starlink closer to new markets while Louisiana

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:13.060
site talks advanced launch options. This is spacex daily, episode 75. Spacex met with

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:18.440
South Africa's independent communications authority for the first time in formal hearings on starlink

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:24.200
licensing. The session addressed spectrum allocation and local ownership rules but produced

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.620
no immediate approval for service. Direct to cell capability remains blocked until

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:35.000
full licensing clears. The outcome determines whether southern Africa joins the growing

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.100
list of regions with starlink coverage. While South Africa weighs ownership rules, spacex

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:47.700
is simultaneously pressing regulators in another major emerging market. SpaceX resubmitted its

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.380
application to India's regulators for the whole second generation starlink constellation. The

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:59.560
filing covers up to 30,000 satellites and includes updated technical parameters for the expanded network.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:05.540
Approval would allow deployment of the higher capacity gen-2 design over Indian territory.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:12.540
The move follows earlier partial approvals that limited satellite numbers. As starlink pushes for

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:17.500
orbital capacity on the ground, new physical launch infrastructure is also advancing.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.500
Louisiana Governor Jeff Landry scheduled a public announcement on a new spacex launch site

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.440
agreement in Iberia Parish. The deal follows the recent dismissal of an Exxon coastal lawsuit

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:35.840
that had challenged the project. The site would add Gulf Coast capacity beyond existing Texas and Florida

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:43.220
pads. Details on pad design and timeline are expected at the event. Local officials had already begun

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.000
environmental reviews for the project. While new pads are prepared on the ground,

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:53.600
an existing starlink satellite just demonstrated a novel way to observe starship in orbit.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.060
A starlink satellite captured video of a starship upper stage during orbital flight.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.300
The footage shows the vehicle after separation and before reentry.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.840
Laser links between the satellite and ground stations enabled the downlink.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:13.460
The demonstration highlights an expanding role for the constellation in supporting starship test

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:19.640
documentation. The same laser mesh network that supported that observation is now being discussed

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:26.500
in the context of large-scale AI workloads. Memphis Mayor Paul Young called for an open session to

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:32.320
address data center power demand and Tennessee Valley Authority rate structures. The meeting would

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:38.260
cover how new facilities affect local grids and industrial customers. All of branch's new zoning

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.760
restrictions add another layer of local limits on where such clusters can be cited.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:48.600
Those power and zoning decisions sit alongside the week's regulatory and infrastructure updates

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:55.300
that continue to shape Starlink's global footprint. Community discussion on our slash space ex lounge

00:02:55.300 --> 00:03:00.360
points to an expected announcement for a space ex facility at Pecan Island, Louisiana.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.780
The location sits near the proposed launch site area under discussion with state officials.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:11.060
No official confirmation has issued but local permitting activity has increased.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:17.340
Australian Space Agency statements confirm ongoing coordination with SpaceX recovery teams

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:23.400
for the upper stage located off Christmas Island. Local wildlife photographer has documented the

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:30.100
vehicle's proximity to shore on August 18. Court filings show SpaceX seeking to keep open a case

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:36.020
involving $1.8 million that left a contractor's account before the firm entered bankruptcy.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.940
One thing worth watching is that South Africa's ICASA hearing produced no licensing decision

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:49.420
despite SpaceX's first formal participation. The authority continues to require local ownership

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:55.020
and spectrum concessions that have delayed service in other markets. Without those approvals,

00:03:55.020 --> 00:04:01.420
Starlink remains unavailable to South African users. Resolution depends on whether SpaceX accepts

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:07.500
the ownership terms or appeals the framework. On the AI front, Mayor Young's call for an open

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:13.700
session on data center power demand and TVA rates directly affects planning for large compute clusters

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:19.400
in the Memphis region. The discussion centers on how new facilities would draw from existing grid

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:25.940
capacity already serving industrial loads. Reports outline internal efforts to tie Starlink capacity

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:32.580
and orbital assets to revenue from AI workloads. From an engineering standpoint, the Starlink satellite

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:38.160
that recorded video of the Starship upper stage during flight demonstrates how the constellations

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:44.580
inter-Satellite laser links can serve as an on-orbit observation network. Each laser terminal must

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:49.940
maintain pointing accuracy across hundreds of kilometers while the host satellite moves at orbital

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:56.340
velocity. The link budget, therefore, depends on narrow beam divergence and rapid reacquisition after

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:02.420
occlusion. Placing the camera payload on an already operational Starlink satellite avoids the

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:07.960
mass and power penalties of dedicated imaging spacecraft, collapsing the marginal cost of the

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:13.600
observation to the incremental power draw of the sensor and downlink. The same architecture could

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.780
later support real-time telemetry relay during reentry or docking events once the laser

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:24.560
mass reaches higher density. This approach trades dedicated hardware for reuse of the existing

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:30.120
constellations communications backbone, a classic first principle substitution of software

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:36.000
defined in pointing and routing for additional physical vehicles. The laser link observation method

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:42.360
also reveals a practical idiot index calculation for space-based imaging. A purpose-built imaging

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:48.040
satellite would require its own propulsion, attitude control, power system, and downlink hardware,

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:54.140
multiplying the raw material and energy cost by a factor of 5-10 compared with adding a modest

00:05:54.140 --> 00:06:00.720
sensor to an existing Starlink platform. By contrast, the incremental cost here is dominated by the

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:05.940
sensor's silicon and the extra kilowatt hours needed to run the camera and route the data through

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:12.180
the laser mesh. That gap shrinks further as laser link density increases because the marginal

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:18.160
energy per additional data stream falls with better routing efficiency. The result is an observation

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:24.560
capability whose finished cost sits much closer to the raw inputs of silicon, optics, and electrical

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:31.200
power than any standalone spacecraft could achieve. Future extensions of this technique could integrate

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:36.880
thermal or spectral sensors to monitor heat shield performance or propellant behavior on the upper

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:42.300
stage without adding mass to the test vehicle itself. The physics constraint remains the same.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:48.160
The host satellites orbital motion and the need for precise beam steering set an upper bound

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:54.000
on dwell time and resolution. Yet the economics favor scaling the approach across dozens of

00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:00.680
Starlink units rather than launching separate assets. Over successive flights, accumulated data from

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:06.520
these opportunistic observations could reduce the number of dedicated instrumentation flights required.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.000
Directly lowering the per-test cost of validating starship reusability milestones.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:18.680
A quick note on the market shows the stock moving modestly higher. Before we go, watch for the Louisiana

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:24.920
announcement details on pad design that could clarify how the new site fits into overall launch cadence.

